from pathlib import Path
import json,html,shutil,hashlib,math
from PIL import Image
I=Path('outputs/deep-water-mechanism-pilot100-20261106/analysis');P=I/'gallery';S=I/'source';S.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
a=json.loads((P/'assessment-data.json').read_text());by={r['case']:r for r in a['cases']};pv={(r['case'],r['layer']):r for r in a['pv']};mom={r['case']:r for r in a['momentum']}
checks={p.stem:json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in I.glob('*-s1.json')}
for name in ['reduce.py','plot.py','extra.py','build_page.py','package.py']:shutil.copy2(Path('work/mechanism-audit/pilot-analysis')/name,S/name)
for name in ['DeepMechanism.jl','PVLayerBudgets.jl','SpectralDiagnostics.jl','production.jl']:
 shutil.copy2(Path('work/mechanism-audit/ql-retry-20261106')/name,S/name)
(S/'README.txt').write_text('Read-only mechanism assessment of six matched, exactly two-dimensional 100Te pilots. reduce.py reads completed outputs on Unity; it performs no state evolution. Dependencies: Python, NumPy, SciPy, h5py. Pass case index 0..5 and output directory. plot.py and extra.py use outputs/deep-water-mechanism-pilot100-20261106/analysis relative to the project working directory; they require Matplotlib and Pillow. build_page.py writes this page. The Julia files document the actual dynamics and diagnostics; production.jl is the two-case QL retry driver, not a general six-case launch script. No launch is authorized by this publication. Original linear/full source digest e7419d08c7abc3009699811beb4f44356ae9869145dc33884e51e2c7899afa6e; corrected QL digest 7acb2f5276e6139d4fae36a13fd98f6ed61722986b6b1b300d0650408bbf9a7d. The fix changes a diagnostic normalization, not the integration operator. Full native fields remain on Unity. Public data contain the displayed spectral crops, evolution, profile samples and full-domain radial transfer curves.\n')
# Save checks without bulky repeated sector rows, and remove non-finite values.
def clean(x):
 if isinstance(x,dict):return {k:clean(v) for k,v in x.items()}
 if isinstance(x,list):return [clean(v) for v in x]
 if isinstance(x,float) and not math.isfinite(x):return None
 return x
validation={c:{k:v for k,v in d.items() if k not in ['spectral_metrics']} for c,d in checks.items()};(P/'validation.json').write_text(json.dumps(clean(validation),indent=2,allow_nan=False)+'\n')
css='body{font:17px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1120px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 22px 60px;color:#193143;background:#f5f7f9}h1{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2.5em}a{color:#135e91}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:white}figure{margin:30px 0}figcaption,.note{font-size:15px;color:#405465}figcaption{padding:12px 3px}.box{background:white;padding:15px 22px;border-left:4px solid #3c799e;margin:25px 0}.limit{border-color:#ba702e}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px;background:white}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd6de;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}details{background:white;padding:14px 20px;margin:20px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}code{font-size:.85em}@media(max-width:600px){body{padding:0 12px;font-size:16px}td,th{padding:6px}}'
h='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Deep-water waves: testing three jet mechanisms</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><a href="../">← Spectral-exclusion gallery</a><h1>Deep-water waves: testing three jet mechanisms</h1><p>Six matched runs · 2048 × 1024 · 100 eddy times · one seed · 6 November 2026</p><nav><a href="#verdict">Assessment</a><a href="#pv">PV</a><a href="#spectra">Spectra</a><a href="#momentum">Momentum</a><a href="#quality">Numerical limits</a><a href="#next">Next tests</a><a href="#data">Data &amp; source</a></nav>'
h+='<div class="box"><strong>All six runs completed.</strong> The cleanest positive result is wave-enhanced mean-flow generation in the quasilinear system, where the nonzero-K eddy–eddy cascade is absent. Broad near-surface PV homogenization is not observed. Directional spectral depletion develops in the fully nonlinear case, but a resolved, curved cascade barrier is not established.</div>'
h+='<div class="box limit"><strong>The late fully nonlinear results are not a converged mechanism test.</strong> At 100 T<sub>e</sub>, the deep-water/control runs place 7.80%/7.49% of their energy in modes with either coordinate wavenumber above 80% of its Nyquist limit. PV variance grows strongly and the physical-transport reference does not explain that growth. Exact diagnostic closure does not remove this numerical limitation. Late plots are retained and labeled so the failure is visible.</div>'
h+='<h2 id="verdict">What holds up?</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Assessment</th></tr>'
h+='<tr><td>PV homogenization generates the jets</td><td>In the top 0.125 depth, final mean-PV variance is 0.976 of its initial value in the full run and 1.107 in QL. RMS gradients are 1.107 and 1.453 of the initial analytic-gradient norm. Early full-run profiles also fail to flatten.</td><td><strong>Not supported as broad-layer homogenization in this pilot.</strong> Thin, localized plateaux remain a separate question.</td></tr>'
h+='<tr><td>An inverse cascade meets a wave-induced spectral barrier</td><td>The full system transfers energy upscale early. At radius 16 cycles, nonlinear inward transfer at 25 T<sub>e</sub> differs by only about 2% between deep water and control when integrated over the whole depth. Upper-layer directional depletion strengthens later, with depth/estimator dependence.</td><td><strong>Inverse transfer and anisotropy: yes. A localized curved barrier: unproven.</strong> Full-depth flux cannot resolve a surface-only barrier, and late small-scale accumulation weakens the evidence.</td></tr>'
h+='<tr><td>Momentum-flux convergence builds mean currents</td><td>QL mean-energy fractions are 5.93% with deep-water waves and 2.03% without them. Native signed stress reconstructs mean advection; its 0.1-T<sub>e</sub> time integral agrees to 0.003% in deep QL and 0.032% in deep full.</td><td><strong>Supported for the simulated mean-flow budget.</strong> Radiation from a source, group propagation, reflection and critical-level absorption are not independently demonstrated.</td></tr></table></div>'
h+='<h2>The matched experiment</h2><p>The surface waves are deep water: u<sup>s</sup>(z) = 0.03125e<sup>8z</sup>, ∂<sub>z</sub>u<sup>s</sup> = 0.25e<sup>8z</sup>, surface-wave k = 4 and decay depth 0.125. The current domain is 0 ≤ x &lt; 4, −2 ≤ z ≤ 0, hence kH = 8. This is an exactly two-dimensional current model with periodic x and impermeable, free-slip vertical boundaries. No constant-gradient case substitutes for this target.</p><p>All six cases use identical saved seed-1 velocities: the 27-cycle ring, width 1, nominal u<sub>0</sub> = 1.563598513 × 10<sup>−4</sup>, T<sub>e</sub> = 37.69911184, and initial U<sup>L</sup> = 0. The physical mean Eulerian current is therefore −u<sup>s</sup> initially in wave cases. Numerics are centered second-order C-grid advection, SSPRK3, explicit viscosity 10<sup>−10</sup>, maximum step 1 and CFL 0.5. These are the approved mechanism pilots; they differ from the earlier WENO runs in the <a href="../deep-water-long/">1000-T<sub>e</sub> gallery</a>.</p><ul><li><strong>Fixed mean:</strong> nonlinear advection is removed and the mean is held fixed. Zero mean growth is imposed, not a physical negative result.</li><li><strong>Quasilinear:</strong> mean–eddy coupling and the K = 0 eddy stress remain, while eddy–eddy forcing of nonzero K is removed.</li><li><strong>Fully nonlinear:</strong> all centered-advection interactions remain.</li></ul>'
h+='<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Case</th><th>E(100)/E(0)</th><th>Mean-energy fraction</th><th>Grid-tail fraction</th></tr>'
for c in ['deep-linear-s1','nowave-linear-s1','deep-ql-s1','nowave-ql-s1','deep-full-s1','nowave-full-s1']:
 r=by[c];h+=f'<tr><td>{c}</td><td>{r["E_final_over_initial"]:.4f}</td><td>{100*r["jet_fraction_final"]:.2f}%</td><td>{100*r["grid_tail_fraction_final"]:.4g}%</td></tr>'
h+='</table></div>'
def fig(name,caption):
 im=Image.open(P/(name+'.webp'));w,hh=im.size
 return f'<figure><a href="{name}.webp"><img src="{name}.webp" width="{w}" height="{hh}" loading="lazy" alt="{html.escape(name.replace("-"," "))}"></a><figcaption>{caption} <a href="{name}.pdf">PDF</a>.</figcaption></figure>'
h+=fig('evolution','Solid: deep-water waves; dashed: matched no-wave cases. Colour identifies model arm. Mean energy is ½〈U²〉. The upper-right ratio uses native full-depth total kinetic energy. Bottom left: energy in modes with |K| or |ℓ| above 80% of the corresponding grid Nyquist wavenumber. Bottom right is a layer-mean energy density divided by initial full-depth energy density, not a fraction of the layer’s total energy.')
h+='<h2 id="pv">PV: little mean flattening, and an energetic constraint</h2><p>We use q = −∂<sub>z</sub>u<sup>s</sup> + ∂<sub>z</sub>u − ∂<sub>x</sub>w, so Q = −0.25e<sup>8z</sup> + U<sub>z</sub>. Mean-profile variance, eddy variance and total layer-centered variance are measured separately on the native PV nodes. Reduced mean-profile variance alone would not establish irreversible mixing.</p>'
h+=fig('pv-profiles','Deep-water cases. Top: Q(z) at 0, 25, 50 and 100 Tₑ; bottom: changes from the initial profile. Showing both prevents the large imposed background from hiding small changes. No smoothing is applied. The full model’s late small-scale structure is numerically suspect.')
h+=fig('pv-tests','Mean-profile variance and RMS mean-PV gradient in three fixed layers. The gradient denominator is the analytic initial s_z norm; the initial discrete value differs from one by about 4 × 10⁻⁵. A persistent, substantial fall would support homogenization. The chosen interior layer also fails that test. These are single-seed time histories, not ensemble statistics.')
h+='<p><strong>There is also an energy limitation, independent of plotting.</strong> If Q is constant in a layer, its mean current must have the form U(z) = u<sup>s</sup>(z) + az + b. Minimizing ½H<sup>−1</sup>∫U² dz over a and b gives an optimistic lower bound on the total energy needed: it permits the entire energy reservoir to become that mean flow and ignores extra boundary/global constraints. The native-grid version enforces U differences from the prescribed s at interior PV nodes.</p><table><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Minimum energy / initial total energy</th></tr>'
for r in a['PV_homogenization_energy_lower_bounds']:h+=f'<tr><td>{r["lower"]:g} &lt; z &lt; {r["upper"]:g}</td><td>{r["ratio_to_initial_total_energy"]:.3g}</td></tr>'
h+='</table><p>Thus exact flat PV across the entire top decay depth is energetically inaccessible in these unforced, nearly energy-conserving runs: its relaxed lower bound is 1.32 times the initial total energy. The top quarter requires 17.7 times as much. This does not rule out thin plateaux or partial flattening; it rules out treating broad homogenization as an automatic outcome of this initial condition. The 0.0625-thick interior layer is energetically allowed yet does not show persistent flattening here.</p>'
h+=fig('pv-resolution-limit','Fully nonlinear cases. Total layer-centered PV variance (left) and eddy PV variance (right; solid top 0.125, dashed top 0.25). The strong late increase is not homogenization. In the deep-water top 0.125 layer, the accumulated half-variance change is +0.00425, versus +0.0000133 from the physical advective transport reference, −0.00114 from explicit viscosity, and +0.00538 from the combined advection/wave remainder relative to that reference. That remainder includes discrete product/flux differences and time quadrature; it must not be labeled physical mixing. QL remainders additionally include deliberately removed interactions.')
h+='<h2 id="spectra">Spectra: early inverse transfer, later directional depletion</h2><p>Below, horizontal Lagrangian velocity appears above its corresponding eddy spectrum. K = 0 is removed before the eddy display. Both cases share the same scale in each figure. The primary comparison uses the top 0.25 depth. There is no fitted exclusion curve: the pilot has not established one.</p>'
h+=fig('full-comparison-25','Single-seed, fully nonlinear snapshots at 25 Tₑ. Horizontal Fourier energies are summed into bins 4 cycles wide, matching the vertical Hann spacing. Grey contours interpolate these binned energies; they add no independent resolution. K = 0 is removed before binning, so the central bin still contains nearby nonzero K. No vertical zero padding or spectral smoothing. The vertical scale of the velocity field is expanded for readability; colours clip at ±3u₀. At this time the deep-water grid-tail fraction is 0.263%.')
h+=fig('full-comparison-100','Same construction at 100 Tₑ. The directional concentration is clearer, but these late fully nonlinear fields have substantial grid-tail energy. They are descriptive evidence, not a converged barrier demonstration.')
h+=fig('spectral-time-means','Fully nonlinear eddy spectra averaged over 10–25 and 50–100 Tₑ, trapezoidally from snapshots every 5 Tₑ (4 and 11 samples). This is time averaging of one seed. Native Fourier bins are shown directly; each row uses a common deep/control maximum. Window D = 0.25, Hann. Linear input ring structure is not an excluded region.')
h+='<details><summary>All six arm snapshots and window sensitivity</summary>'
h+=fig('snapshots-deep','Deep-water snapshots at 100 Tₑ. Columns: fixed-mean linear, QL and fully nonlinear. Velocity above native-bin eddy spectra for D = 0.25 and 0.125. The common normalization is the largest D = 0.25 eddy-mode energy across all six cases; values above the displayed maximum saturate. Local spectra use collocated velocities and Hann weighting divided by its mean square. The linear ring remains largely untransferred; its empty interior is not proof of an inverse-cascade barrier.')
h+=fig('snapshots-nowave','Matched no-wave snapshots, with the same normalization and geometry as the deep-water panel. These controls are essential: QL mean-flow growth also occurs without imposed waves.')
h+=fig('window-sensitivity','Deep/control ratio of the horizontal-sector fraction within the indicated nonzero-K annulus: |K|/κ ≥ √3/2. Solid: Hann; dashed: even/odd reflection without taper, used only as an estimator sensitivity check. Reflection imposes artificial parity at the window edge and does not create independent vertical observations. Reflected ℓ = 0 is excluded from the angular test. A ratio below one means directional depletion, not necessarily suppressed cascade flux. Linear low-band ratios can be dominated by very small leakage into bands below the initial ring.')
h+='</details><p>In the top 0.25 at 25 Tₑ, the 4–16-cycle horizontal fraction is essentially unchanged (wave/control 1.03 Hann, 0.98 reflected); in 16–24 it is reduced (0.88, 0.73). At 100 Tₑ the corresponding ratios are 0.56/0.48 and 0.53/0.64, but the numerical limitation has grown. At D = 0.125, direct vertical spacing is 8 cycles; at D = 0.25 it is 4. Meanwhile the imposed PV gradient varies by e and e² across those supports. More cells alone cannot remove this localization–spectral-resolution tradeoff.</p>'
h+=fig('nonlinear-flux','Exact native full-depth modal decomposition of the saved tendencies. Π(r) = −Σκ≤r Re(v̂*·N̂), so negative means nonlinear input into low-radius modes. Solid: total nonlinear advection; dashed: its retained eddy–eddy part. Blue deep water; orange no waves. Native cosine/sine transforms preserve the staggered-grid energy norm; no local-window flux is inferred from this plot. The early inverse transfers are similar. Their late sign reversal occurs in both runs and accompanies grid-scale accumulation, so it is not evidence for a wave-specific barrier.')
h+='<h2 id="momentum">Momentum: the budget works; the wave-carrier attribution is unfinished</h2><p>Native stress is formed at the staggered-grid locations and its signed all-K cospectrum reconstructs the physical stress to roundoff. For evolving-mean arms, U growth is dominated by −∂<sub>z</sub>〈ũw̃〉. Integrated U is conserved to roundoff; direct mean Stokes and pressure contributions are negligible. The 0.1-Tₑ sampled stress integral is checked independently against exact accumulated Runge–Kutta mean-advection increments. Integrated R U<sub>z</sub> is positive, accounting for mean-energy growth up to small viscosity/quadrature corrections.</p>'
h+=fig('momentum-budget','Deep-water mean velocity at 100 Tₑ and exact accumulated advection/viscosity contributions (top). The close overlay confirms the mean-momentum budget. Bottom: signed stress averaged over 50–100 Tₑ for deep water and control; vertical profiles are not phase/group-velocity measurements. The fixed-mean linear arm is excluded from this closure test because its nonlinear mean stress feedback was deliberately removed.')
h+=fig('momentum-cospectra','Signed stress by horizontal wavenumber and depth, averaged over the 51 integer-time outputs from 50–100 Tₑ using trapezoidal weights. A symmetric logarithmic colour scale retains both signs and small values. No quadrant mirroring is used to infer propagation. A stress-carrying eddy need not be a freely propagating vortex wave.')
h+='<p>The QL comparison demonstrates that an eddy–eddy inverse cascade among nonzero K is not necessary for mean-current growth in this setup. It does not show that full-system jets are predominantly generated by radiating vortex waves: QL changes the available nonlinear dynamics, and the no-wave QL control also generates mean flow.</p><p>The <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2606.00443v1#S2.SS1">Vallis–Matilsky–Nicolas source-radiation argument</a> requires identifiable waves propagating away from a source. This pilot starts with a depth-distributed random ring, rather than a localized source. We have not independently measured packet group velocity, established reflection at a turning level, or demonstrated critical-layer absorption. Using the assumed dispersion relation to infer group velocity from the stress sign would be circular. Those parts remain untested here.</p>'
h+='<h2 id="quality">What the numerical checks do—and do not—establish</h2><p>All six cases have 1001 dense diagnostic outputs and 101 full-velocity times, with full tendency checkpoints at 0, 10, 25, 50 and 100 Tₑ. Original array 66829261 completed the four linear/full cases. The QL cases initially failed at time zero because a pressure-work identity was normalized by cancellation-level work. Array 66837635 reran only those two cases after an actual-state regression and deliberate corrupted-flux rejection test; the physics and stepping operators were unchanged.</p><p>Independent SciPy transforms reproduce the native kinetic-energy norm to below 10⁻¹⁴ relative error. Offline centered-advection reconstruction matches the stored component fields. Online energy and mean-momentum identities close near roundoff. These establish bookkeeping consistency, not resolution or PV conservation by the discrete nonlinear scheme. The grid-tail energy grows from 0.008% at 10 Tₑ to 0.263% at 25, 1.27% at 50 and 7.80% at 100 in deep full. In deep QL it is 0.0228% at 100. One resolution and one seed cannot establish convergence or reproducibility.</p>'
h+='<h2 id="next">What would discriminate the mechanisms next?</h2><ol><li><strong>Fix the numerical evidence before extending full turbulence.</strong> Hold the deep-water profile and initial condition fixed, compare resolutions and explicitly controlled dissipation with a formulation that controls PV/enstrophy error. Predefine acceptable grid-tail and PV-budget behaviour. The present late centered-advection result cannot justify simply integrating longer.</li><li><strong>Test the momentum-wave claim with a localized packet.</strong> In the same exponential background, measure propagation independently from the packet envelope; compare measured signed stress with measured group velocity, then test source/sink mean acceleration. Turning-depth and critical-layer tests need their own controlled background/absorption conditions.</li><li><strong>Choose a feasible PV hypothesis.</strong> Preselect thin layers whose minimum homogenization energy fits the available energy, then require persistent flattening, scalar/variance evidence and a controlled budget. Broad surface-layer homogenization requires a different energy regime and is a different experiment.</li><li><strong>Test the spectral barrier with a local transfer budget.</strong> Resolve early low-K eddy–eddy input, mean exchange and vertical pressure/advection transport separately; compare depletion against that budget across windows. A dumbbell overlay or an anisotropic image alone is insufficient.</li></ol><p>No new simulations are launched by this assessment. Any follow-up simulation needs a separately specified and confirmed setup.</p>'
h+='<h2 id="data">Downloads and reproducibility</h2><p><a href="assessment-data.json">Numerical assessment</a> · <a href="validation.json">Configuration and checks</a> · <a href="case-metrics.csv">Case metrics</a> · <a href="pv-metrics.csv">PV budgets</a> · <a href="momentum-metrics.csv">Momentum budgets</a> · <a href="homogenization-energy-bound.csv">Energy bounds</a> · <a href="spectral-metrics.csv.gz">Angular/window metrics</a></p><p><a href="https://github.com/npizzo/wave-current-gallery/tree/main/scripts/deep-water-mechanism-pilot">Analysis and model source</a>. Full native fields and dense diagnostic archives remain on Unity. Public figure data are listed below.</p><p><a href="data/">All spectral files by case, window and time</a> · <a href="data-manifest.json">Data checksums</a></p><details><summary>Evolution, profile and flux files</summary><ul>'
for p in sorted((P/'data').glob('*')):
 if not p.is_file():continue
 h+=f'<li><a href="data/{p.name}">{p.name}</a> ({p.stat().st_size/1024:.0f} KB)</li>'
h+='</ul><p>Spectral files retain both signed wavenumbers, linear per-bin energy, every plotted window/estimator and the stated snapshots/averages in the crop |K|/(2π), |ℓ|/(2π) ≤ 40. They are neither normalized nor clipped. Evolution files use 0.1-Tₑ sampling. Profile files use 0, 10, 25, 50 and 100 Tₑ. Radial flux files are native full-domain cumulative component work, not a local cascade flux.</p></details><p class="note">The experiments and assessment here are exactly two-dimensional. No claim about three-dimensional turbulence follows from this pilot. The manuscript has not been edited.</p></body></html>'
(P/'index.html').write_text(h)
print('Built',P/'index.html')
